I added the `--DRY_RUN` support. `parseFlags` now recognizes `DRY_RUN` (bare or `=value`), and `main` branches on its presence: it validates config via the existing `loadConfig`, writes one `dry-run port=<port> level=<level> capacity=<capacity>` line, and returns `{ exitCode: 0, config }` with no queue. Invalid configs still hit the existing error path and return `exitCode: 2` before any queue is built. Added valid, bare-flag, and invalid dry-run tests in `test/app.test.js`; all 31 tests pass and only those two files changed.
